Given, capacitance, $C=10^{-6} \mathrm{~F}$
Inductance, $L=10^{-4} \mathrm{H}$
Frequency of oscillation of $L-C$ series resonant . circuit,

\begin{aligned}
f & =\frac{1}{2 \pi \sqrt{L C}}=\frac{1}{2 \pi \sqrt{10^{-4} \times 10^{-6}}} \\
& =\frac{1}{2 \pi \times 10^{-5}}=\frac{10^5}{2 \pi} \mathrm{Hz}
\end{aligned}

Given, $L=0.5 \mathrm{mH}=0.5 \times 10^{-3} \mathrm{H}$ and $C=20 \mu \mathrm{F}=20 \times 10^{-6} \mathrm{~F}$
The resonant frequency of $L-C$ circuit is
$\begin{aligned}
f &=\frac{1}{2 \pi \sqrt{L C}}=\frac{1}{2 \pi \sqrt{0.5 \times 10^{-3} \times 20 \times 10^{-6}}} \\
&=\frac{1}{2 \pi \times \sqrt{10 \times 10^{-9}}}=\frac{10^{4}}{2 \pi}=1592.3 \simeq 1592 \mathrm{~Hz}
\end{aligned}$

